    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d42">

                <pb facs="0056" n="46" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg46"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">7510.92/216: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Saigon</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Flood</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Saigon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-01-28T14:00:00+07:00">January 28, 1941—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:23 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8. An agreement between Thailand and Indochina to cease hostilities became
                    effective at 10 o’clock this morning and armistice negotiations are scheduled to
                    begin here tomorrow.<anchor n="62" xml:id="d42-f1"/> The Thai delegation is
                    expected from Bangkok by Japanese plane this afternoon and General Sumita<anchor
                        n="63" xml:id="d42-f2"/> is arriving by plane from Hanoi. A Japanese cruiser
                    and a smaller vessel of the several Japanese warships observed off Cap Saint
                    Jacques during the past 3 days are also expected at Saigon this afternoon.</p>
                <p>Sent to Cavite for repetition to the Department; Chungking, Peiping, Hong Kong,
                    Shanghai. Hong Kong please repeat to Tokyo. Repeated to Bangkok.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Flood</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d42-f1" n="62" xml:id="d42-f1-content">
                <p>In his telegram No. 11, February 1, 11 a.m., Consul Flood reported to the
                    Department the signing of the Thai-Indoehinese armistice on January 31 at 6 p.m.
                    (751G92/227).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d42-f2" n="63" xml:id="d42-f2-content">
                <p>Maj. Gen. Raishiro Sumita, Chief of the Japanese Military Mission to French
                    Indochina and Chairman of the Truce Conference at Saigon.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
